 "description": "Screen the companies StockLens scores nightly by region, exchange, sector, industry, market-cap band and trading volume, sorted by one of the six StockLens scores or by market cap, volume, popularity or ticker, and return the top or bottom N. This is the only StockLens tool that ranks or compares companies: use it for any top N, best, worst, highest, lowest or filtered request, and never build such a list from get_market_summary or general knowledge. It has no valuation, price-target or growth filter; say so rather than calling a score sort one. status ranked means the requested order was used. browse_substituted means a score order was asked for and market-cap order with scores hidden was returned, so never describe those rows as ranked by score. locked means no companies are named; relay message verbatim. What the caller can sort and how far it reaches is in access_tier and reach_capped_at. Report only the rows returned. It does not trade and gives no personal recommendations.",
